WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.520
French president Emmanuel Macron has condemned
as 'inexcusable' the brutal repression of

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.780
Algerian protesters by Paris police 60 years
ago.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:16.640
On October 17, 1961, officers carried out
a deadly crackdown on a demonstration by tens

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.290
of thousands of Algerians, in one of the darkest
episodes in post war France.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:28.579
Some historians say more than 200 people were
killed in the violence.

00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:33.160
It's the first time a French president has
attended a memorial ceremony for the Algerians

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.000
killed on that night.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.930
Emmanuel Macron joined relatives of the victims
in paying tribute.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:46.400
60 years ago at this spot, bodies were fished
out from the Seine river.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:53.010
An estimated 25 thousand Algerians rallied
peacefully in protest against a curfew imposed

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.920
on them alone.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.470
Police responded without mercy, arresting
nearly 12-thousand and killing dozens, throwing

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.649
their bodies into the river.

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:07.729
Many others were taken away to sorting centers
and then deported.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:13.270
Said Abtout was there that night.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.360
"The police came.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.690
When we they got to us, they started to massacre
people, hitting them with batons on the head,

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:25.979
then kicking them in head with their shoes
on.

00:01:25.979 --> 00:01:28.940
I'd never seen anything like that."

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:34.000
The violence occurred in the final year of
France's violent attempt to keep Algeria as

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.890
one of its colonies.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:40.490
For decades, successive administrations ignored
the massacre.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:45.030
President Macron's condemnation of the killings
was only issued in a written statement and

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:47.299
did not include an apology.

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:51.979
This year's commemoration took place amid
diplomatic tensions between both countries

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:53.079
over their history.

